#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d3d8e8c-7015-514a-83d5-689d89928164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d3d8e8c-7015-514a-83d5-689d89928164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330962} :answer-field/id #uuid "71eec172-b52c-5418-b4c8-f8193b53a4fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1907cff1-d30a-5b75-824e-0f4eeed40d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1907cff1-d30a-5b75-824e-0f4eeed40d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330964} :answer-field/id #uuid "93924ffb-a290-5db3-a9aa-c4a3471f00b8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be33203-eb3d-5b59-b741-3172d9bd920c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4be33203-eb3d-5b59-b741-3172d9bd920c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d8b4fb-dea8-5833-96e3-217d302463fc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1df841d-233d-5571-b2fe-b548c0a2b431" :question/math-academy-id "q-316725" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/assets/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-1-3\\text{i})-x(-1+3\\text{i})+(-1+3\\text{i})(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+10) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+10x-2{x}^{2}-4x-20) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+6x-20) & = \\\\ -2{x}^{3}-12x+40 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}-12x+40.$"}]}
